hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7240","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Jaafar bin Darastuwaih Al-Farisi told us, Abu Yusuf Yaqoub bin Sufyan told us, Abu Tawba Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ al-Halabi, Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir told us, on the authority of al-Abbas ibn Salim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Amr ibn Absa, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. The first time he was sent, he was in Mecca, and at that time he was in a state of disdain. I said: What are you? He said: “I am a prophet.” I said: What is a prophet? He said: “Messenger of God.” I said: What did he send you with? He said: “That God is worshiped, and idols are broken, and relatives are connected through righteousness and ties.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7240 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7241","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Ibrahim bin Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Madani Al-Shajri, my father told me, on the authority of Abd bin Yahya, on the authority of Muadh bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’ Al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father Rifa’ah Ibn Rafi’, and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He and his cousin Muadh Ibn Afra went out until they reached Mecca. When they came down from the hill, they saw a man under a tree - he said: This was before the six Ansar left - he said: so when we saw him, we spoke to him. So we said: We will bring this man and bid him farewell until we circumambulate the Kaaba. We greeted him with the greetings of pre-Islamic times, and he responded to us with the greetings of the people of Islam. We heard about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but we disapproved, so we said: Who are you? He said: “Come down.” So we went down and said: Where is the man who claims and says what he says? He said: “I,” and I said: “Then present it to me.” So he presented Islam to us and said: “Who created the heavens and the earth and the mountains?” We said: God created them. He said: “Who created you?” We said: God. He said: “Who made these idols that you worship?” We said: We.He said: “The Creator is more deserving of worship than the creation. You are more deserving that you should be worshiped even though you did them, and God is more worthy that you should worship Him than Something you did and I call to the worship of God and the testimony that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God and the connection of the womb and the abandonment of aggression. By enraging people.” We said: No, by God, if what you are calling for were false, it would be among the lofty affairs and good morals. So hold our mount until We came to the house, and Muadh bin Afra sat next to him. He said: So I came to the house, went around and took out seven cups, and made a cup of them for him. So I faced the house and said: O God, if what Muhammad is calling for is true, then he brought out his cup seven times, so I struck it and it came out seven times. So I shouted, “I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” The people gathered around me and said: A crazy man who has become a youth. I said: Rather, a man of faith. Then I came to the top of Mecca, and when Muadh saw me, he said: Rifa’ah has come with a face the likes of which he has never seen, so I came. I believed and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us Surat Yusuf.And recite in the name of your Lord who created. Then we went out to return to Medina, and when we were at Al-Aqiq, Muadh said: I have never gone to my family at night, so I spent the night. with us until the morning, and I said: I refused, and with all the news I have with me, I would not have done it. And Rifa’ah was when he set out on a journey and then presented himself to his people. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7241 - Yahya Al-Shajri is the author of Munakir"
"7242","Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad told us Bin Hisham bin Malas al-Numayri told us, Marwan bin Muawiyah al-Fazari told us, Abu Abdullah al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin al-Hasan told us, Abu Asim and Makki bin Ibrahim, they said: Bahz bin Hakim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, who is more righteous? He said: “Your mother.” I said: Then who? He said: “Your mother.” I said: Then who? He said: “Your father.” I said: O Messenger of God, then who? He said: “Then the closest, then the closest.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it on their condition in Hakim bin Muawiyah on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of His father said: I said: O Messenger of God, who is most righteous? He said: “Your mother.” I said: Then who? He said: “Your mother.” I said: Then who? He said: “Your mother.” I said: Then who? He said: “Then your father, then the closest, then the closest.” Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “Then we found evidence for this hadith, including them.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7242 - True"
"7243","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh did not tell us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr told us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ubaid bin Ali, on the authority of Khadash bin Salamah, a man of the Companions, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will advise a woman “I will entrust a man to his mother, and I will entrust a man to his father, and I will entrust a man to his master, to the one next to him, even if there is harm upon him, he will harm him.” And among them is “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7243 - It has evidence"
"7244","Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Al-Sakouni did not tell me, in Kufa, Abdullah bin Ghannam told me, my father told me, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told me, Mus’ar bin Kadam narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Utbah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, which people have the greatest right to The woman? He said: “Her husband.” I said: Which people have greater rights over a man? He said: “His mother” and from her."
"7245","What Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Al-Masoudi told us, about Iyad bin Luqit, on the authority of Abu Rimthah, said: I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard him say: “Honor your mother, your father, and your sister.” And your brother, then we are nearer to you, more nearer to you” and from her “"
"7246","7246 - Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub did not tell us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Buhair Bin Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, God God Almighty advises you to do the closest, then the closest.” Ismail bin Ayyash, one of the imams of the people of the Levant, was only displeased with his bad memory. And among them “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7246 - We only resent Ismail for his poor memory"
"7247","What Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Saghani told us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I slept and you saw me in Paradise.” So I heard the voice of a reader reading, and I said: Who is this? They said: Haritha bin Al-Nu’man. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ‘Such is righteousness.’ He was the most righteous of people towards his mother. ‘This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not take it out in this context.” Ibn Uyaynah and others said about it: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Paradise and did not They mention sleep in him, but he does not honor his mother.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7247 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7248","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, in Marwa, Abu Qalaba told us, H. Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hasan bin Sahl Al-Mujawiz told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Muhammad bin Talha bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Jahimah, Jahmah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I wanted to go on a campaign and I came to consult you. He said: Do you have a mother? He said: Yes, he said: “Go and stick to her, for Paradise is at her feet.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7248 - True"
"7249","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Harun bin Sulaiman told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, and Ahmad bin Jaafar told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The satisfaction of the Lord is in the satisfaction of the father, and the anger of the Lord is in the wrath of “The Father” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7249 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7250","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Qantari told me, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and he told us Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, and Abu Hudhayfah, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have come to pledge allegiance to you on Migration and I left my parents crying. He said: “Then go back to them and make them laugh as you made them cry.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it was not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7250 - True"
"7251","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: He married a man and his mother disliked that, so he came to ask Abu al-Darda’, and he said: Divorce the woman and obey your mother, for I will I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The mother is the middle of the gates of Paradise, so put that away or keep it.” Narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Ata bin Al-Sa'ib, explained with explanation
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7251 - True"
"7252","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, that a man was ordered by his parents or one of them to divorce his wife, so he appointed a thousand freed men or One hundred freed, and he does not have a gift if he does so. He came to Abu al-Darda’ and mentioned that he had prayed the forenoon prayer. Then he asked him and said: Fulfill your vow and be kind to your parents, for I will I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The father is the middle of the gates of Paradise. If you wish, then guard the gate or leave it.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7252 - True"
"7253","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed me, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Ibn Abi informed me A wolf, my uncle Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, he said: I was under a woman I like her. Omar hated her, so he said to me: Divorce her, but I refused. Then Omar came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have Abdullah bin Omar had a woman whom I hated, so I ordered him to divorce her, but he refused, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Abdullah bin Omar! Divorce your wife and obey your father.” Abdullah said: So I divorced her. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7253 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7254","Abu Saeed Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Ahmad bin Yahya bin Ishaq Al-Halwani told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd told us Al-Aziz bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hani, the client of Ali bin Abi Talib, that Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: Oh Hani, what do people say? He said: They claim that you have knowledge from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but you do not reveal it. He said: Without the people? He said: Yes. He said: Show me the sword, so I gave him the sword, and he took out from it a scroll containing a book. He said: This is what I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Cursed.” “God curses whoever sacrifices to other than God and whoever turns to someone other than his followers, and God curses the one who disobeys his parents, and God curses the one who diminishes the lighthouse of the earth.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7254 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7255","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad Al-Faqih told me about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledging his pledge of allegiance to migrate, and he said: I I came to pledge allegiance to you on migration and I left my parents crying. He said: “Go back to them and make them laugh as you made them cry.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”"
"7256","Muhammad bin Saleh and Ibrahim bin Asma told us, saying: Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Khuzaymah, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Muhammad bin Hilal told us, Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b bin Ujrah told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ujra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Bring “The pulpit.” He attended us, and when he ascended one step he said: “Amen.” When he ascended the second step, he said: “Amen.” When he ascended the third level, he said: “Amen.” When he descended, we said: O Messenger of God, we heard from you today something that we had not heard before. He said: “Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, presented to me He said: After the time of Ramadan, and he has not been forgiven. I said: Amen. Then when I performed the second ruqyah, he said: After the one before whom you were mentioned, but he did not pray for you. I said: Amen. Then when I recited the third ruqyah, he said: After all, for one whose parents, or one of them, has reached old age and does not admit him to Paradise, I said: Amen. This is A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7256 - True"
"7257","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayoub, on the authority of Zaban bin Faid, on the authority of Sahl bin Muadh, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He who is righteous “Blessed is his father. May God increase his life.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7257 - True"
"7258","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Yahya bin Hakim, and Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Sarraf told us, they said: Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Pardon the wives of the people, and your wives will be chaste, and be kind to your fathers, and your children will be blessed. And whoever comes to his brother disavowing him, let him accept that from him, and he is right. Or it is invalid, and if he does not do that, he will not return to the basin.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7258 - Rather, it is weak"
"7259","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid al-Asadi al-Hafiz, and Abdan ibn Yazid al-Daqqaq al-Hamdanian, told us about Hamdan, saying: Ibrahim ibn Al-Hussein bin Dizel, Ali bin Qutaybah Al-Rifai told us, Malik bin Anas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Be kind to your fathers, and your children will be kind to you, and pardon people’s wives, and your wives will be chaste. And whoever is disobedient to him, it will not be accepted.” He did not come to the basin for me.”"
"7260","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Mufid, told us: Ahmed told us Bin Muhammad bin Nasr, Abu Nu`aym al-Fadl bin Dukayn told us, Abd al-Rahman bin al-Ghaseel bin Suleiman told us, H Al-Hasan bin Halim told me Al-Marwazi, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Usayd bin Ali, on the authority of Ubaid al-Saadi, on the authority of His father, that he heard Abu Usayd Malik bin Rabi’ah Al-Sa’idi, may God be pleased with him, saying: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when A man from Banu Salamah came to him and said: O Messenger of God, is there anything left of my kindness to my parents that I can do to them after their death? He said: “Yes, praying for them, asking forgiveness for them, fulfilling their covenants, and honoring their friend and relative of the kin, for whom you have no kin except from “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission before them, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7260 - True"
"7261","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Daoud Al-Zahid told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Junaid told us, Sahl bin Othman Al-Askari told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Muhammad bin Suqa narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Oh Messenger of God, I have sinned many sins. Do I have any repentance? He said: “Do you have parents?” He said: No. He said: “Do you have a maternal aunt?” He said: Yes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Then he treated her kindly.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7261 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7262","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad told me, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she said: “A woman from the people of Dumat al-Jandal came to me. She came seeking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after his death, asking him about the recent About something she entered into from the matter of sorcerers, she did not act on it.” Aisha said to Urwa: “O my sister’s son, I saw her crying when she did not find the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to heal her. I even To have mercy on her, while she said: I am afraid that I have perished. I had a husband, but he was absent from me, and an old woman came in and I complained to her, and she said: So you did what I commanded you, and perhaps it would come to you. When night came, she came to me with two black dogs, and I rode one of them and the other, but I could not stay. Until we stopped in Babylon, and I saw two men hanging by their feet, and they said: What brings you? So I said: I am learning magic. They said: We are a test, so do not disbelieve and go back. I refused and said: No. They said: Go to that oven and urinate in it. I went and was terrified. But I did not do so, so I went back to them and they said to me: Did you do it? I said: Yes. They said: Did you see anything? I said: I did not see anything.They said: You did not do that. Go back to your country and do not become an infidel. So I refused. They said: Go to that oven and urinate in it. So I went and my skin shivered. I was afraid, then I returned to them and they said: What did you see? I said: I did not see anything. They said: You lied. You did not do it. Go back to your country and do not become an infidel, for you are in charge of your affairs. I refused, so they said: Go to that oven. So I urinated in it, so I went and urinated in it, and I saw a knight masked with iron coming out of me until he went into the sky and disappeared from me until I could not see him, so I came to them. I said: I did, and they said: So what did you see? I said: I saw a knight masked with iron come out from me and go into the sky and disappear from me until I could not see anything. They said: You have spoken the truth. Your faith has left you. Go. So I said to the woman: By God, I do not know anything, and they did not say anything to me. They said: Yes, if you want. Nothing but take this wheat and sow it. So I sowed, and I said: Sprout, and it sprung, and I said: Is it ripe, so I sowed? Then I said: Sprout, so it sprout, then I said: Sprout, so it sprout. Then I said: Ground it, and it withered. Then I said: Grind it, and it ground. Then I said: Bake, and it baked. When I saw that I did not want anything, it fell into my hand. And I regretted it, by God, O Mother of the Believers, I have never done anything and I will never do it.So I asked the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the recent death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while they were available that day, but they did not know what They say to her, and they are all terrified and afraid that he will give her a fatwa with what he does not know, except that they said: If your parents, or one of them, were alive. They would have been enough for you. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it. The purpose of narrating it in this situation was the consensus of the Companions. Two hadiths.” The death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The parents are sufficient for her.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7262 - True"
"7263","Ali bin Hamshadh, Al-Adl - may God Almighty have mercy on him - and Abdullah bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, saying: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Issa Ibn al-Tabba’, Bakkar Ibn Abd al-Aziz Ibn Abi Bakra told us, he said: I heard my father, narrating on the authority of Abi Bakra, may God be pleased with him. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “All sins, God will postpone whatever He wishes of them until the Day of Resurrection, except disobedience to parents.” “For God Almighty will hasten it to its companion in life before death.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7263 - Bakkar bin Abdul Aziz is weak"
"7264","Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them he said: “They hated to make concessions to their lineages, and they were polytheists, so the verse was revealed: {It is not upon you to guide them} [Al-Baqarah: 272] - until it reached - {And what And spend of good, for God is All-Knowing of it.} [Al-Baqarah: 273] So He made a concession to them.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7264 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7265","Abu Bakr Ahmad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Harun, Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God Almighty said: I am the Most Merciful, and it is the Most Merciful. So whoever joins it, I will join it, and whoever breaks it, I will cut it off.” “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.” It was narrated with clear chains of transmission on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Sa`id ibn Zayd ibn Amr bin Nufail, Aisha, and Abdullah bin Amr """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7265 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7266","So Abu Ja`far Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Hafiz informed us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein informed me, and Abu Muhammad Al-Muzani informed me, praising Ali. Ibn Muhammad al-Ja’ani, they said: Abu al-Yaman told us, Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, Abdullah bin Abi al-Hussein told us, Nawfal bin Musahaq, on the authority of Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The womb is a shield from the Most Gracious, so whoever maintains it May God bless him and whoever breaks it, God Almighty will cut him off.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7266 - True"
"7267","Ahmad bin Salman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hisham Al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abu Kathir, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Qariz, that his father told him that he had visited Abd al-Rahman bin Awf while he was sick. Then Abdul-Rahman said to him: You are a relative. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God Almighty said: I am the Most Merciful, and she is the uterus, I have torn apart.” “It has a name from my name, so whoever joins it, I will join it, and whoever sever it, I will sever it, and whoever divides it, I will sever it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7267 - True"
"7268","Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdul-Hamid Al-San’ani told me about Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, Abdul Razzaq informed me, Muammar informed me, Al-Zuhri told me, Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman told me, that Raddad Al-Laythi told him on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Awf, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of him, he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God, Blessed and Most High, said: I am the Most Merciful. I created the womb and divided it from My Name.” So whoever connects it, it will connect it, and whoever breaks it, it will be left alone. “This is Abu Raddad Al-Laythi, to which Sufyan bin Uyaynah and Muhammad bin Abi Ateeq have added, And Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, and Sufyan bin Hussein.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7268 - True"
"7269","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, we told him: Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Abu Al-Raddad complained, and Abdul Rahman came to him returning and said: The best of them and the most sincere, as far as I know. Abu Muhammad, and Abdul Rahman said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God Almighty said: I am God and I am the Most Merciful. I created the womb.” “And I divided my name for it, so whoever joins it, I will join it, and whoever breaks it, I will cut it off.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7269 - True"
"7270","As for the hadith of Muhammad bin Abi Ateeq
 So Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Fadl Al-Asfati and Al-Hasan bin Ziyad told us, they said: Ismail bin Abi told us. Uwais, my brother Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Abu Raddad Al-Laythi, told him on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may God be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “God said Blessed and Most High: I am the Most Merciful. I created the womb and divided it from My Name. So whoever joins it, I will join him, and whoever sever it is his father.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7270 - True"
"7271","So Abu Sahl bin Ziyad the grammarian told me, in Baghdad, Abd al-Karim bin al-Haytham told us, Abu al-Yaman told us, Shuaib told us, H told us, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, and the pronunciation for him is: Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili narrated to us, Bishr bin Shuaib narrated to us, my father told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman told me that Abu al-Raddad al-Laythi told him, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf mention that he heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “God, Blessed and Most High, said: I am the Most Merciful. I created the womb and divided for it from My name. So whoever joins it, I will connect it.” And whoever cuts it, I will cut it off.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7271 - True"
"7272","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, Abu al-Raddad al-Laythi, may God be pleased with them both. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God Almighty said: I am the Most Merciful. I created the womb and divided for it a branch of My Name. He joined it, I continued it, and whoever broke it, I cut it off. “I returned to the mention of the Companions, may God be pleased with them all.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7272 - True"
"7273","So Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us, Abu Ismat Sahl bin Al-Mutawakkil told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, he told me Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Muzard, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The womb is a protection from God - he meant a protection from the name of God, the name that is Most Gracious - whoever joins it, connects it, and whoever breaks it cut it off
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7273 - True"
"7274","So Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi informed us, saying: Othman bin Saeed told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Qaboos, said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr, referring it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Those who are merciful will have mercy on them.” May God have mercy on the people of the earth, and the people of heaven will have mercy on you. The womb is a branch of the Most Gracious, so whoever joins it will connect it, and whoever severes it will sever it.” Al-Hakim said. May God Almighty have mercy on him: “All of these hadiths are authentic, but I investigated their chains of transmission by mentioning the Companions, may God be pleased with them, lest Someone is under the illusion that the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, did not neglect the authentic hadiths.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7274 - True"
"7275","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Hudhayfah, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him. He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in a red cloak of about forty men, and he said: “It is open to you and you.” They will be helped and correct. So whoever of you realizes that, let him fear God, and enjoin what is right, and forbid evil, and maintain His mercy, and like the one who He helps his people in ways that are not right, like the example of a camel that stumbles back, so it trails with its tail.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7275 - True"
"7276","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San’ani told us, Zayd ibn al-Mubarak told us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman told us Ibn Masmoul, Al-Qasim Ibn Makhaul Al-Nahdi told us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he heard his father say: I said: Oh Messenger of God, advise me. He said: “Establish the prayer, pay the zakat, fast during Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House, perform Umrah, honor your parents, be kind to your relatives, acknowledge the guest, and enjoin kindness.” “And he abstained from evil and strayed from the truth wherever it strayed.” The chain of transmission is authentic by the sheikhs of Yemen, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7276 - Ibn Masmoul is weak"
"7277","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmed bin Al-Sammak told us, in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Yahya told us Bin Saeed Al-Qattan, on the authority of Awf, and Abi Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl, Yahya bin Abi Talib narrated to us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata narrated to us, Awf bin Abi Jamila reported, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, he flinched. people to him, and it was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and I came among the people to look at him. When I saw the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I knew that his face was not the face of a liar, so the first thing he said was: “O people, spread your greetings, serve food, and pray.” The relatives and pray at night while the people are asleep. You will enter Paradise in peace.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"7278","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told me, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammam told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Maimuna, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, if I see you, my soul becomes happy and my eyes are happy, so tell me about Everything. He said: “Everything was created from water.” He said: I said: Inform me of a matter that, if I act upon it, I will enter Paradise. He said: “Spread peace and feed “Food, connect the relatives, and spend the night while the people are asleep, then enter Paradise in peace.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7278 - True"
"7279","Ibrahim bin Firas al-Faqih told us about Mecca, which God Almighty protected, Bakr bin Sahl told us, Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told us, Sa`id bin Sahl told us. Bashir, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “It is written in the Torah who “His desire is for his life to be prolonged and for his livelihood to be increased, so that he may maintain his ties of kinship.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it in this context, rather they agreed On the hadith of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7279 - True"
"7280","So Abdullah bin Ja’far Al-Ashri told us, Ya’qub bin Sufyan told us, Mahdi bin Abi Mahdi Al-Makki told me, Hisham bin Yusuf told us. Al-San’ani, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever is pleased with God’s provision of his life, and expand his livelihood for him, and ward off from him an evil death, so let him fear God and maintain his mercy.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7280 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7281","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, Abdullah bin Salih told me, Al-Layth told me, Ibn Al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sarari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Hussein, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, said: “Whoever is pleased that his life will be prospered and his livelihood expanded for him, let him maintain his ties of kinship.” Mawqoof
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7281 - Suspended"
"7282","Abu Jafar Al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Othman Al-Basri told us, Imran bin Musa Al-Ramli, who is the son of Abi Imran, told us, we told us Abu Khaled Suleiman bin Hayyan Al-Ahmar, Dawud bin Abi Hind told me, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God will grant the people long life and increase for them wealth, and He has not looked upon them since He created them with hatred for them.” They said: How is that, O Messenger of God? He said: “By their ties to their relatives.” Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “Imran al-Ramli was one of the ascetics of the Muslims and their servants. He memorized this. “The hadith on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar is strange and authentic.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7282 - Imran bin Musa Al-Ramli was the only one to memorize it, and if he memorized it, it is authentic."
"7283","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Ishaq bin Saeed bin Amr ibn al-Aas, my father told me, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, when a man came to him and she died to him with a uterus a long way away, and he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Know your lineages and maintain your ties of kinship, for there is no closeness to a kinship if it is severed, even if it is near or distant.” “It is hers when she arrives, even if she is far away.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7283 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7284","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari informed us, Abu Al-Mawjih informed us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Issa. Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Yazid, the client of Al-Manba’th, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Learn from your lineages. “Whatever you use to connect your relatives, for the connection of relatives is love for one’s family, enrichment in money, and longing for one’s legacy.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7284 - True"
"7285","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he told me Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Zuhar, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, who said: I met The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I turned to him and took his hand, and he turned to me and took my hand and said: “O Uqba, shall I not tell you of the best manners?” The people of this world and the hereafter. “You will maintain ties with those who cut ties with you, give to those who deprive you, and pardon those who wronged you. And whoever wants to extend his life and expand his livelihood, let him maintain ties with him.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7285 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7286","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Othman Al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Majeed Al-Hanafi, Muawiyah bin Abi Muzard told me, my uncle Abu Al-Hubab Saeed bin Yassar told me, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Indeed, God Almighty, when He had finished creating, the womb rose up and took hold of the loins of the Most Merciful, and He said: Mh. She said: This is the place of the one who seeks refuge with you from estrangement. Then he said: Are you not satisfied that I should maintain the ties with you and sever the ones who cut off your ties? “Recite, if you wish, ‘If you were to take charge, would it be that you would spread corruption on earth? And sever your ties of kinship} [Muhammad: 22] to his saying: {Do they not contemplate the Qur’an?} [An-Nisa’: 82] etc. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7286 - This in Al-Bukhari"
"7287","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Amr bin Marzuq told us, Shu’bah told us, and he told me Ahmad bin Musa al-Faqih, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, they said: Muhammad bin Ja`far told us, Shu`bah, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abdul-Jabbar narrating on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “The womb is a curse from the Most Gracious that says: O Lord, I have been cut off. Indeed, I have been wronged, O Lord. Then its Lord answers it and says: Are you not satisfied? “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7287 - True"
"7288","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Hibban and Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, they said: Hammad told us Bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The kin will come on the Day of Resurrection, having a hilt like the hilt of a spindle, and he speaks with a fluent, fluent tongue. He joins whoever joins it and cuts off whoever.” “He cut it off.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7288 - True"
"7289","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Musa bin Sahl bin Kathir told us, Ismail bin Ulayya told us, Uyaynah bin Abd told us. Al-Rahman bin Jawshan Al-Ghatfani, my father told me, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no “A sin that is more likely to be punished by God, along with what He has in store for him in the Hereafter, than transgression and severing ties of kinship.” It was narrated by Shu’bah, On the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7289 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"7290","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Muammar bin Sahl told us, Issa told us, on the authority of Yunus, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard my father, speaking on the authority of Abu Bakra al-Thaqafi, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no sin.” It is more likely and more worthy that God Almighty bestows for his companion the punishment in this world along with what He has in store for him in the Hereafter of severing ties of kinship and transgression.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7290 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"7291","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Saeed bin Salem told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Sharhabeel Ibn Muslim means that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Hijra is not permissible for more than three days. They met and one of them greeted the other, and the other returned the greeting. They shared in the reward, but if the other refused to return the greeting, this man would be absolved of his sins. Sin is an epidemic that causes the other - and I think he said - and if they die while emigrating, they will not meet in Paradise. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7291 - True"
"7292","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Yahya bin Abi Masarra told us, Abdullah bin Al-Muqri told us, Haywa bin Shuraih told us, Abu Uthman bin Abi Al-Walid told me that Imran bin Abi Anas told him on the authority of Abu Kharash Al-Sulami, may God be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “Whoever abandons his brother for a year will have his blood shed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7292 - True"
"7293","Ishaq bin Saad bin Al-Hassan bin Sufyan told us, in Bansa, Jeddi told us, Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who is your master, my son? “Slaves?” They said: Al-Jadd bin Qais, because he was stingy. He said: “And what disease is more cured than stinginess? Rather, your master and the son of your master is Bishr bin Al-Baraa bin Ma’roor” This hadith is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it, and Sa’id bin Muhammad is Al-Warraq, trustworthy and trustworthy, and we wrote it down from the hadith Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salamah"
"7294","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Ubaid Allah told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub, Abu Asim told us, Ja’far bin Yahya bin Thawban told us, on the authority of his uncle Amara bin Thawban, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a scarab, and a woman came to him, and I was a boy on that day. When she approached the Messenger of God, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he spread out his robe for her and she sat on it. I said: Who is this? They said: This is his mother who breastfed him. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7294 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"7295","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Maruzi informed me, Abu Al-Mujah told us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Haywa bin Shurayh informed us, Sharhabeel bin Muslim told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of companions “In the sight of God, the best is to his neighbor, and the best of neighbors in the eyes of God is the best to his neighbor.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7295 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7296","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Malik bin Anas, and Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Mahran told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman told us, He said: I heard Malik bin Anas, speaking on the authority of Saeed al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Shurayh al-Kaabi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever He believes in God and the Last Day, so let him honor his guest by giving him a reward for a day and a night, and hospitality for three days, and beyond that, it is charity and does not It is permissible for him to stay with him until he brings him out - Ibn Wahb added in his hadith - and his reward is that he should present to him the best of what he finds today.” He said: “Yathwi: He stays with him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. The narration about it was also authentic on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and I think they narrated it. What I have is that the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, neglected the hadith. Abu Shurayh, based on the narration of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7296 - It is authentic on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and I think they narrated it"
"7297","As Abu Abdullah Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Mufaddal told us, Abdul Rahman told us Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever believes By God and the Last Day, let him be generous to his neighbor.” And mentioning the hadith to its end, Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: “Then I heard Ali bin Isa say: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq say: Malik bin Anas memorized this chain of narration from a number like Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq. Abdul Hamid bin Jafar followed Malik bin Anas, in his narration"
"7298","Bundar told us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, Abdul Majeed bin Jaafar told us, Sa`id al-Maqbari told us, that he heard Abu Shuraih say: My ears heard it, my eyes saw it, and my heart understood it when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke about it. Then he mentioned the hadith like the hadith of Malik. Either way: “As for the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, not one of them used Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq as evidence.”"
"7299","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abu Dhib, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And God does not believe, and God does not believe.” And God does not believe. They said: What is that, O Messenger of God? He said: “A neighbor from whose calamities his neighbor is not safe.” They said: What are his calamities, O Messenger of God? He said: “His evil.” This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, and they did not narrate it in this context.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7299 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7300","Abu Al-Abbas told us, after him, he said: Bahr bin Nasr told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told me, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Sinan Ibn Saad Al-Kindi, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not “A believer is he whose neighbor is not safe from his attacks.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7300 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7301","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Ya’la and Muhammad told us, Ibn Ubaid, Aban bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sabah bin Muhammad Al-Bajli, on the authority of Murrah Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God has divided among you your morals as He has divided among you your livelihood, and God gives money He loves and whoever does not love, and He does not give faith except to the one who loves, then whomever God has given faith has loved, and by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, he will not submit. A slave until his heart is at peace, and no slave is safe until his neighbor is safe from his harms.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7301 - True"
"7302","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Bakra Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his neighbor complained to him, and he said: O Messenger of God, my neighbor is hurting me. So he said: “Take out your belongings and place them on the road.” So he took out his belongings and placed them on the road, and everyone who passed by said: What is your business? He said: I complained about my neighbor to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered me to take out my belongings and place them on the road. They started saying: Oh God. Curse him, O God, disgrace him. He said: Then the news reached that man, so he came to him and said: Go back, and by God I will never harm you. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. And he did not bring it out.” And he has another authentic witness, according to Muslim’s condition.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7302 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7303","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharza told us, Ali ibn Hakim told us, a partner told us, on the authority of Abu Omar Al-Azdi, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, complaining about his neighbor, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Throw your belongings on the road.” He said: Then people began to pass by him and curse him. Then he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of God. By God, what people did I meet? He said: “And what did I meet among them?” He said: They curse me. He said: “God has cursed you before the people.” He said: O Messenger of God, I will not return. He said: Then the one who complained came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Have you believed or have you been cursed?”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7303 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7304","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Yahya, Mawla Ja`dah said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: It was said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: So-and-so prays and fasts at night. day, and there was something on her tongue that would hurt her neighbors. He said: “There is no good in her. She is in Hell.” And he was told: So-and-so prays the obligatory prayers and fasts. Ramadan, and she gives alms to the bulls, and has nothing else for her, and does not harm anyone. He said: “She will be in Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7304 - True"
"7305","Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Hilal ibn al-Ala al-Raqi told us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Raqi told us, Musa ibn Ayyan, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Yahya, the client of Ja'dah bint Hubayra, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: It was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him: So-and-so fasts during the day and stays up at night and hurts her neighbors with her tongue. He said: “There is no good in her. She is in Hell.” It was said: So-and-so is She prays the obligatory prayers, fasts Ramadan, gives alms of harvested wheat, and does not harm anyone with her tongue. He said: “She will be in Paradise.”"
"7306","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Ayyash Al-Ramli told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan told us on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Jamil, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Abdul Harith, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Part of the happiness of a Muslim person in this world is “A good neighbor, a spacious house, and a comfortable boat.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, for Jamil is the servant of Abdullah bin Al-Harith. Al-Ansari, Habib bin Thabit narrated from him without a hadith.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7306 - True"
"7307","Yahya bin Mansour Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Salamah told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Bashir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Musawar, said: I heard Ibn Abbas, and he was miserly to Ibn al-Zubayr and said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believer who spends the night with his neighbor next to him is not hungry.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. This is witnessed by Omar’s conversation with Saad when he built the palace that “
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7307 - True"
"7308","Ahmad ibn Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah, said: It reached Omar that when Sa’d built the palace, he said: The sound stopped, so Muhammad bin Maslamah sent to him - The hadith, and at the end of it he said - Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: I hated to order you to be cold and for me to be hot, while the people of Medina were around me. Hunger killed them, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A man is not satisfied without his neighbor.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7308 - Its chain of transmission is good"
"7309","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told us, Musa bin Harun told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, Ja’far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juni, on the authority of Yazid ibn Babunus, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, I have two neighbors, with which one should I start? He said: “By the one closest to you by the door.” This is how he narrated it on the authority of Ja’far bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu Imran Al-Juni, and the correct narration is Shu’bah’s narration, On the authority of Abu Imran al-Juni, on the authority of Talha ibn Abdullah, a man from Banu Taim Allah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: I said: Oh Messenger of God, I have two neighbors, to which of them should I give a gift? He said: “To the one closest to you in door.” This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, for Talha bin Abdullah bin Awf was among those who agreed on ""Getting it out""
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7309 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7310","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Haywa told me, On the authority of Ibn al-Haad, that al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham told him on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “You will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to what you love one another over?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “Spread peace among yourselves and love one another, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you have mercy on one another.” They said: O Messenger of God, we are all merciful. He said: “It is not the mercy of any one of you, but the mercy of the common people.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7310 - True"
"7311","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abu Hani Humaid bin Hani Al-Khawlani, Abu Saeed Al-Ghafari told me that he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “My nation will be afflicted by the disease of nations.” They said: O Messenger of God, what is the disease of nations? He said: “Naughtiness, arrogance, arrogance, quarreling in this world, hatred, and envying people to the point of transgression.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it is not “He brings him out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7311 - True"
"7312","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of my father Yahya bin Abi Sulaym said: I heard Omar bin Maymun, narrating on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Whoever is pleased to find the taste of faith, let him love a person and love him only for the sake of God Almighty.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. """"
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7312 - True"
"7313","Professor Abu Al-Walid and Abu Bakr bin Quraysh told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Quta’i told us, and Muhammad Bin Abi Bakr Al-Muqaddami and Nasr bin Ali, they said: Ruh bin Ata told us, Sayyar Abu Al-Hakam told us, that Khaled bin Abdullah testified. Al-Qusri, while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit in Basra, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Yazid bin Asad, do you love Paradise? I said: Yes. He said: “Then love for your Muslim brother what you love for yourself.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and Yazid bin Asad bin Kurz was a companion of the Prophet. He resided in Basra.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7313 - True"
"7314","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, and Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan told us Al-Hamdani, Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Kharraz narrated to us, saying: Ishaq bin Sulaiman Al-Razi narrated to us, saying: I heard Malik bin Anas, speaking on the authority of my father Hazim bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, he said: I entered the Damascus Mosque and behold, a young man with bright complexions, and behold, the people were with him when they disagreed. Concerning something, they attributed it to him and proceeded from his opinion, so I asked about it, and it was said: This is Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, and the next day I left. I found him praying before me. He said: So I waited for him until he finished his prayer, then I came to him in front of him and greeted him and said: By God, I love you for the sake of God. He said: By God? So I said: By God? He said: By God, and I said: By God. He said: Then he took hold of my cloak and pulled me to him and said: Give good news, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “God Almighty said: My love is obligatory for those who love one another for My sake, and those who sit together for My sake, and those who exchange each other for My sake, and those who visit one another over My sake.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. Abu Idris combined, with an authentic chain of narration, between Muadh and Abbad ibn al-Samit in this text.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7314 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7315","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyid told us, my father told me, Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Ibn Halbas, on the authority of Abu Idris, may God forbid, who said: A man passed by, and I stood up to him and said: This man narrated to me the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Did you hear him? That is, Mu'adh. He said: He was only speaking to you in truth, so I told him. He said: I heard this from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, meaning about those who love each other. In God, God will shade them in the shade of His Throne on the Day when there will be no shade but His shade, and nothing is better than it. I said: Yes, may God have mercy on you, and what is better than that? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrating on the authority of God Almighty. He said: “It is true. My love is for those who love one another for Me, My love is true for those who are in continuity with Me, My love is true for those who visit one another for Me, My love is true for those who exchange each other for Me.” And I do not know. With whichever one he started. I said: Who are you, may God have mercy on you? He said: I am Ubadah ibn al-Samit. “This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7315 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7316","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Saeed bin Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, Ahmad bin Ja’far told us Al-Qutay’i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ya’la, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, said: I sat in a gathering in which were twenty of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and lo, among them A young man with a beautiful face and good age. I am pleasing to the eyes and enticing to the cheeks. If they disagree about anything or say something, they end up with what he said. He is Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him. The next day, I came and saw him praying at a pillar. He stopped praying, then hid himself, and I remained silent. So I said: I love you for the glory of God. He said: “By God.” I said: By God. He said: “For those who love one another for the sake of God - he said: I think he said - in “God’s shadow on the Day when there will be no shade except His shadow.” Then he said - and there is no doubt about the rest of it -: “Thrones of light will be placed for them, which will bless them with their sitting from the Lord.” Blessed and Most High are the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs.” He said: So I narrated it to Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and he said: I will not narrate to you except what I heard on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My love is true for those who love one another for My sake, My love is true for those who exchange hands for My sake, and My love is true for those who deal with each other.” in me, and my love for those who visit one another is confirmed in me, and my love for those who are in continuity is confirmed in me.” Shu’bah doubted about those who are in continuity and visitors in me. “This is an authentic hadith based on The condition of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.” It was narrated by Ata’ al-Khurasani, on the authority of Abu Idris al-Khawlani."
"7317","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Ibn Jabir told me, Ata Al-Khurasani told us, He said: I heard Abu Idris Al-Khawlani say: I entered the Homs Mosque and sat in a group, all of them speaking about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And among them was a young boy who, when he spoke, the people listened to him, and if he spoke to one of them, they listened to him. Then they dispersed, and I did not know who that boy was. Then he mentioned the hadith in its length
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7316 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7318","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, in Isfahan, Abu Badr Shuja’a told us Ibn al-Walid, he said: I heard Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, narrating on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Allah has servants who are neither prophets nor martyrs. The martyrs and prophets will envy them on the Day of Resurrection because of their closeness to God Almighty. And their sitting is from Him.” Then a Bedouin knelt down on his knees and said: O Messenger of God, describe them to us and make them lawful to us. He said: “A group of people who were close to each other due to tribal conflict, who became friends with God and loved each other for Him. God Almighty will set for them on the Day of Resurrection platforms of A light that people fear but do not fear. They are the guardians of God Almighty, upon whom there is no fear nor do they grieve. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7318 - True"
"7319","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq told us in Baghdad, Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us Al-Anazi, Musa bin Wardan told me that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A person is The religion of his friend, so let one of you see who he is with.” It was narrated on the authority of Abu al-Hubab Sa`id ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah"
"7320","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Lakhmi told us, Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, Sadaqa bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad Al-Ansari, on the authority of Saeed bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A person follows the religion of his friend, so let each one of you look to whom he differs from.” The hadith of Abu al-Hubab is authentic, God willing, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7320 - It is true, God willing"
"7321","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told me, in Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Musa bin Daoud Al-Dhabi told us, Al-Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, On the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, he said: A man passed by the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and a man said: I love him for the sake of God Almighty. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did you know him?” He said: No. He said: “Then teach him.” He said: I met the man and informed him. He said: “I love you because you have loved me.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. The hadith of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karb witnessed it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7321 - True"
"7322","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Habib bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If “If one of you loves his brother, let him know it.”"
"7323","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Abu Asim told us, Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No two men love each other for the sake of God Almighty except that the better of them loves them more strongly.” To its owner: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7323 - True"
"7324","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Sukkari told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Hakam Al-Arni told us, Sulayman bin Abi Sulayman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, She said: O Messenger of God, I am so-and-so, the daughter of so-and-so. He said: “I have known you, so what is your need?” She said: My need is that my cousin so-and-so is a worshipper. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have known him.” She said: He is proposing to me, so tell me what is true. The husband has a duty over his wife. If there is something I can tolerate, I will marry him, and if I cannot tolerate it, I will not marry. He said: “It is the husband’s right over the wife if he sheds blood.” And if it were necessary for a human being to prostrate to another human being, I would have commanded the wife to prostrate. For her husband when he enters upon her because God Almighty has favored him over her. She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not marry as long as I remain in this world. A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7324 - Rather, Suleiman is the Yamani. We have weakened him"
"7325","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum Al-Isfahani told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us Al-Dastawi, my father told me, Al-Qasim bin Awf Al-Shaybani told me, Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, told us that he came to the Levant and saw the Christians. They prostrate to their bishops, priests, and patriarchs, and he saw the Jews prostrating to their rabbis, monks, rabbis, and scholars. And their jurists, and he said: Why are you doing this? They said: This is the greeting of the Prophets, may blessings and peace be upon them. I said: We have more right to do what we do with our Prophet. Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, they lied to their prophets just as they distorted their book. If I had ordered anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have ordered the woman to prostrate to her husband because of his great right over her, and no woman will find sweetness. “Faith until she fulfills her husband’s rights, even if he asks her herself while she is on the back of a camel.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7325 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7326","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abd Al-Aziz bin Al-Khattab told us, Hibban bin Ali told us, on the authority of Saleh bin Hibban, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraydah, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, teach me something that I will gain from it. Certainly. He said: So he said: “Leave that tree.” So he called for her, and she came until she greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he said to her: Go back, so she went back. He said: Then he gave him permission and kissed his head. And his feet, and he said: “If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7326 - Indeed, it is false"
"7327","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Jafar told us Bin Yahya, on the authority of Amara bin Thawban, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best of you “The best of you is for women.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7327 - True"
"7328","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman told us Al-Dhabi, Musawar bin Abdullah Al-Himyari narrated to us, on the authority of his mother, who said: I heard Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Any woman who dies and her husband is satisfied with her will enter Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7328 - True"
"7329","Muhammad bin Ali Al-Shaybani told me, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No “A woman fasts while her husband is a witness, except by his permission.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7329 - True"
"7330","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Mandah al-Asbahani told us, Bakr bin Bakkar told us, Omar bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Two, do not exceed Their prayers are their heads: a slave who absconds from his master until he returns, and a woman who disobeys her husband until she returns.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7330 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7331","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Humaid bin Ayyash Al-Ramli told us, Ma’mal bin Ismail told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a woman with two girls who had become pregnant. One of them was leading the other, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pregnant mothers are merciful, had they not come to their husbands.” “The women who prayed will enter Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not take it out. “Shu’bah narrated it, on the authority of Al-A’mash
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7331 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7332","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Abu al-Walid told us, and Muhammad bin Kathir told us: We told us: Shu'bah, and Abu Bakr bin Balawayh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu'bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja'd, who said: It was mentioned to me on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, that a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, had two sons with her, so he gave her three dates. She gave each one of them a date, then one of the boys cried, so she broke it. So she gave each of them half, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pregnant mothers are merciful to their children if it were not for what they do.” By their wives, the ones who prayed will enter Paradise.”"
"7333","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad, the grammarian, told me in Baghdad, Al-Hasan ibn Makram told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of my father Please, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, woman was created from a rib and you “If you want to live in it, you can break it and live in it” three times. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7333 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7334","This is witnessed by the hadith of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Woman was created From a crooked rib, and if you straighten it you will break it, and if you leave it you will live by it while there is crookedness in it.” This is an authentic chain of transmission according to Muslim’s condition. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7334 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7335","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us, with Marwa, Abu Qalaba Al-Raqqashi told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, Omar bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “No “God looks at a woman who is not grateful to her husband and she cannot do without him.” It was said on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, connected"
"7336","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Ali bin Al-Abbas Al-Bajli told us, Al-Abbas bin Yazid Al-Bahrani told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “No “God looks at a woman who is not grateful to her husband, and she is not in need of her husband.” This is an authentic hadith, according to the two sheikhs’ conditions, if he memorizes it. Al-Abbas, for I heard Abu Ali say: The preserved hadith is from the hadith of Shu’bah.”"
"7337","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq did not tell us, Abu Musa told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Sa’id Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, said: “God does not look at a woman who is not grateful to her husband.” And she cannot do without him.”"
"7338","Abu Al-Qasim Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Uqba bin Khaled Al-Sakouni informed us of Kufa, Ubaid bin Ghannam bin Hafs bin Ghayath, my father told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Utbah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: O Messenger of God, who is one of the greatest people? right on women? He said: “Her husband.” I said: Who has the greatest right over a man? “His mother” said, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7338 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"7339","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Mubarak bin Fadalah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas May God be pleased with him. He said: Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought something, he would say: “Take it to so-and-so, for she was a friend of Khadija. “Take him to so-and-so, for she loved Khadija.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7339 - True"
"7340","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to slaughter a sheep and follow it.” Sadiqa Khadija bint Khuwaylid, may God be pleased with her: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7340 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7341","Ahmad ibn Kamil al-Qadi told us, Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Narsi told us, Ruh ibn Ubadah told us, Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Were it not for the Children of Israel, no woman would have cheated on meat, and had it not been for Eve, no woman would have cheated.” “Her husband.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7341 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7342","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Abu Awanah told us, Daoud bin Abdullah Al-Awdi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Makki, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Qais, who said: I invited Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him. He got up one night, grabbed his wife, hit her, and then called me, “Oh Ash’ath.” I said: Here you go. He said: Learn from me three things that you learned from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not ask a man why he beats his wife, nor “You ask him about one of his brothers whom he relies on and does not rely on them, and do not sleep except on the basis of Witr.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7342 - True"
"7343","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khorasani Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Ubaid Al-Nahwi told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abu Bakr Al-Taymi, he said: On the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of his father, that an Arab man, called Ufeir, used to cheat on Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr: O Ufeir, what did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say about love? He said: I heard him say: “Friendliness is inherited and hatred is inherited.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And it was narrated by Yusuf ibn Attiya, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7343 - There is a break in the report"
"7344","Abu Al-Fadl Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Muzaki told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Yusuf bin Attiya, on the authority of Abu Bakr al-Maliki, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr, he said: He met Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, an Arab man called Ufeir. Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said to him: What you heard from the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, what does he say about love? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Friendliness and enmity are inherited.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7344 - Yusuf bin Attiyah perished"
"7345","Azhar bin Ahmad bin Hamdoun Al-Harami told me, in Baghdad, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Musa bin Ali bin Rabah said: I heard my father mentioning, on the authority of Suraqa bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not direct you to “Charity, or among the greatest acts of charity, is your daughter’s return to you. She has no one to earn but you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7345 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7346","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Sinan Al-Qazzaz told us, Hammad bin Masada told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Omar bin Nabhan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever has three daughters and is patient with... For their wives and their wives, God will admit him into Paradise by His mercy upon them.” He said: Then a man said: And two daughters, O Messenger of God? He said: “And two daughters.” A man said: O Messenger of God, and one? He said: “And one.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7346 - True"
"7347","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Praiseworthy, he narrates on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by some of his companions and a young boy who was on the road, and when His mother saw the beast and was afraid for her son to have intercourse with her, so she ran to her knees and said: My son. So she carried her son, and the people said: O Prophet of God, what is the matter? This woman was about to throw her son into the fire. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No, by God, God will not throw His beloved into the Fire.” He said: So the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, disputed with them “this.” An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7347 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7348","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf, Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Abu Malik told us Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever gives birth to He did not have intercourse with a woman, nor did he forbid her, nor did he prefer his son - meaning the male - over her. God admitted him into Paradise because of her.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7348 - True"
"7349","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl bin Daughter Ibrahim bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muslim bin told us Ibrahim, Abdul Rahman bin Fadalah told us, Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he said: She came A woman went to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, asking questions, and she had two boys with her, so she gave her three dates, so she gave each boy one date. She grabbed a date for herself, and the boys ate the two dates. So she went to the date, cut it in half, and gave each boy of hers half a date. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and I told him, and he said: “What amazes you about her? God has shown her mercy when she was a child.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7349 - True"
"7350","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, he told me Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz Al-Rasibi, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah bin Anas, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Whoever supports two female slaves until they come to one another, he and I will enter Paradise like these two - and he pointed with his index and middle fingers - and two doors. Their punishment in this world will be hastened: transgression and disobedience.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7350 - True"
"7351","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Hairi told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, Fitr bin Khalifa said: I was sitting with Zayd bin Ali, may God be pleased with him, in Medina, when a sheikh called Sharhabeel Abu Saad passed by him. Then Zaid said to him: Where did you come from, Abu Saad? He said: From the governor of the city. I narrated to him a hadith. He said: So narrate it to the people. He said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There is no Muslim who has two daughters, and he does good to them as long as they are his companions or theirs, but they will admit him to Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7352","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us: Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Nasr, Abu Nu’aym told us, Fitr told us, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said something like this: “This is an illusion, for this Sharhabeel is: Abu Saad Sharhabeel bin Saad, a sheikh from the people of Medina.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7351 - Sharhabeel bin Saad Wah"
"7353","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abu Sakhr told me, on the authority of Ibn Qusayt, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does not have mercy on our young and knows the rights of He is our eldest, so he is not of us.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “The last book of righteousness and connection.”
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7353 - True"
